The CLI runs with the blank-line cap disabled (maxConsecutiveBlankLines
default 0), so source runs of blank lines inside a procedure pass through
unchanged; only the procedure boundary is normalized
(fmt.max_consecutive_blank_lines issue #37, fmt.blank_lines_between_procs).
Whitespace-only lines become empty (fmt.trim_trailing_whitespace).
Note: the style guide's no_excess_blank_lines asks for 3+ blank lines to
become one; the catalog keeps the cap opt-in, so this records the default.
-- input.ssl --
:PROCEDURE Spaced;
:DECLARE nFirst, nSecond;
nFirst := 1;



nSecond := 2;
  
:RETURN nFirst + nSecond;
:ENDPROC;


:PROCEDURE Next;
:RETURN 0;
:ENDPROC;
-- format --
:PROCEDURE Spaced;
	:DECLARE nFirst, nSecond;

	nFirst := 1;


	nSecond := 2;

	:RETURN nFirst + nSecond;
:ENDPROC;

:PROCEDURE Next;
	:RETURN 0;
:ENDPROC;
-- diagnostics --
-- diagnostics [--strict --info] --
